task: sentence_full_enrichment
instructions: |
  Produce learner enrichment for each sentence: natural English, literal
  translation, register, tokens, and words. Tokens are visible word occurrences;
  words are explanation entries referenced by token word_id.

  Hard rule: tokens and words are word entries only. Do not include spaces or
  punctuation as entries, and do not attach punctuation to Hindi or roman
  strings. Every token must have a word_id that matches one words[].id. If a
  visible word repeats, include repeated tokens and reuse the same word_id when
  the explanation is the same.

  Bad token:
    hindi: "हैं?"
    roman: "haĩ?"
    word_id: "w1"

  Bad word:
    id: "w2"
    hindi: ","
    roman: ","
    meaning: "comma"

  Good token:
    hindi: "हैं"
    roman: "haĩ"
    word_id: "w1"

  Good word:
    id: "w1"
    hindi: "हैं"
    roman: "haĩ"
    meaning: "are"

  Return raw YAML only. Do not wrap the response in markdown fences. Do not add
  prose before or after the YAML.

  Required shape:
  results:
    - id: "0001"
      english: "..."
      literal: "..."
      register: standard
      tokens:
        - hindi: "..."
          roman: "..."
          word_id: "w1"
      words:
        - id: "w1"
          hindi: "..."
          roman: "..."
          meaning: "..."
items:
{{#each items}}
  - id: "{{id}}"
    hindi: "{{hindi}}"
    romanisation: "{{romanisation}}"
    english: "{{english}}"
{{/each}}
